<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mangalesha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 592–610</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mangalesha was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badami">Badami</a> from about 592 to 610, ruling after his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirtivarman-i">Kirtivarman I</a>. He defeated the Kalachuris of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahishmati">Mahishmati</a> and conquered Revatidvipa on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a>, and he dedicated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a> cave temple at Badami in 578. He was overthrown and killed by his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pulakeshin-ii">Pulakeshin II</a> in a war of succession.</p></div>
